hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17992","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Dawud, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Abu Zayd, freedman of Thalabah, from Maqil ibn Abi Maqil al-Asadi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade facing the two prayer directions with urine or excrement."
"17993","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Maqil ibn Abi Maqil al-Asadi, he said, My mother wanted to perform Hajj, and her camel was lean. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said, Perform Umrah in Ramadan, for an Umrah in Ramadan is like a Hajj."
"17994","Affan narrated to us, he said, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Zayd, from Maqil ibn Abi Maqil al-Asadi, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade facing the two prayer directions with excrement or urine."
"17995","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Zayd, from Maqil ibn Abi Maqil, that he said, O Messenger of Allah, Umm Maqil missed Hajj with you. He said, So she went out when she missed Hajj with you. He said, Let her perform Umrah in Ramadan, for an Umrah in Ramadan is like a Hajj."
